/// Drains the `biometricEnabled` mirror's own round trip (repository ->
/// `Stream.multi`'s forwarding subscription -> cubit's `emit()` ->
/// `BlocBuilder`'s rebuild, several microtask hops deep) with a handful of
/// plain `tester.pump()` calls — NOT `pumpEventQueue()`, which schedules its
/// own recursive zero-duration `Timer`s and, empirically, never resolves
/// inside this widget-test binding (observed hang); `pumpAndSettle()` alone
/// doesn't help either, since it only keeps pumping while a *frame* is
/// already scheduled, which the first hop hasn't triggered yet.
Future<void> _drainStreamMirror(WidgetTester tester) async {
  for (var i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
    await tester.pump();
  }
}

